        "content": "Now let me solve the problem.\n\n**Setting up:** From $f''_{yy}(x,y)=4$, integrate twice in $y$:\n$$f_y'(x,y)=4y+\\varphi(x),\\quad f(x,y)=2y^2+y\\,\\varphi(x)+\\psi(x).$$\n\nUsing $f_y'(x,0)=\\sqrt2 x$: $\\varphi(x)=\\sqrt2 x$.\nUsing $f(x,0)=x^2$: $\\psi(x)=x^2$.\n\nSo $f(x,y)=x^2+2y^2+\\sqrt2\\,xy$.\n\nOn $x^2+2y^2=4$, we get $f=4+\\sqrt2\\,xy$. So we maximize/minimize $xy$ subject to $x^2+2y^2=4$.\n\nLet $x=2\\cos t,\\ y=\\sqrt2\\sin t$. Then $xy=2\\sqrt2\\sin t\\cos t=\\sqrt2\\sin 2t$, so $\\sqrt2 xy=2\\sin 2t$.\n\nThus $f=4+2\\sin 2t$, giving max $6$, min $2$.",
